                <pb facs="0363" n="278" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg278"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">814.51/300: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Thurston</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-07-30T18:00:00-06:36"><hi rendition="#italic">July 30, 1919,
                                6 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received August 1, 6
                            p.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Prof. Kemmerer and assistant arrived Guatemala July 20. He was immediately
                    received by President Cabrera and now informs me his [progress] to date quite
                    satisfactory.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thurston</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
